<title>Data deletion instructions — Planner</title>
<style>body{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:46rem;margin:4rem auto;padding:0 1.5rem;line-height:1.7;color:#111827}a{color:#6948D7}</style></head>
<body><main><h1>Request deletion of connected social data</h1>
<p>If you connected Facebook or Instagram using Meta, you can revoke Planner's access and send a deletion request through your Facebook <strong>Settings &amp; privacy → Settings → Apps and websites</strong> page. Meta forwards the signed request to Planner. Planner supplies a private confirmation number and status link.</p>
<p>You can also disconnect individual connected accounts from Planner's brand social-account settings. A disconnect alone does not necessarily erase data or revoke a shared provider grant.</p>
<p>Data deletion requests are processed against the social identities we can verify. Where business-authored content, compliance records, or unrelated authorizations are involved, we may need to review applicable retention obligations and will keep the deletion status open until resolved.</p>
<p>For other providers, use their connected-app authorization settings to revoke access; Planner's provider-specific erasure workflows will be added as their requirements are verified. This page does not claim that these providers share Meta's signed callback.</p>
</main></body></html>
